From: SingleAxis Fabric maintainers
Subject: [extension/bearertokenauth] drop empty entries from token files

bearertokenauth's refreshToken() splits a token file on newlines and keeps
every entry after trimming, including empty ones. A blank line or a trailing
newline therefore mints a "" token, which the gRPC path authenticates as the
literal header "Bearer " — an empty credential that bypasses authentication
for any deployment whose token file ends in a newline (the natural output of
`openssl rand -hex 32 > token` and most editors).

Drop entries that trim to empty and warn when any were removed, so file
formatting can never mint a credential. An all-empty file now yields zero
tokens (every request rejected) instead of one empty token (every request
with a blank credential accepted).

--- a/extension/bearertokenauthextension/bearertokenauth.go
+++ b/extension/bearertokenauthextension/bearertokenauth.go
@@ -156,10 +156,16 @@ func (b *bearerTokenAuth) refreshToken() {
 		return
 	}
 
 	tokens := strings.Split(string(tokenData), "\n")
-	for i, token := range tokens {
-		tokens[i] = strings.TrimSpace(token)
+	kept := tokens[:0]
+	for _, token := range tokens {
+		if trimmed := strings.TrimSpace(token); trimmed != "" {
+			kept = append(kept, trimmed)
+		}
+	}
+	if dropped := len(tokens) - len(kept); dropped > 0 {
+		b.logger.Warn("dropped empty token entries from file",
+			zap.String("filename", b.filename), zap.Int("dropped", dropped))
 	}
-	b.setAuthorizationValues(tokens) // Stores new tokens
+	b.setAuthorizationValues(kept) // Stores new tokens
 }
